{
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "i. e. when two things known to be quite different from each",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "other are identified together to show their great resemblance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "to each other the fig. is Rüpaka.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 21. क्षान्तिश्चेत्—cf. क्षमाशस्त्रं करे यस्य दुर्जनः किं करिष्यति ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "कवचेन—is undoutedly a better reading. The other reading",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "वचनेन means ‘why need conciliatory words’ i. e. these are super-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "fluous. क्रोधः— Anger itself is a great enemy as it causes much",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "restlessness and worry to a man ज्ञाति &c.—Because the dâyâdas",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "are a fire that internally consumes. हृदय becomes हृत् after सु or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "दुर् when the sense is ‘a friend or a foe’; ( see com. ); अन्यत्र",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "सुहृदयः; दुर्हृदयः । Sid. Kau. अनवद्या—न अवद्या ( न वद्या अवद्या ) अनवद्या",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "blameless, commendable and not अभिचारादिविद्या. Mark the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "difference of meaning between अवद्य and अनुद्य both formed by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "the aff. य: the former means what is not fit to be spoken, what",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "deserves blame; the latter ‘what ought not to be named; as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "अवद्यं पापं, अनुद्यं गुरुनाम. See Kau. on Pan. III. 1. 101, अवद्यप-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "ण्यवर्या गर्ह्यपणितव्यानिरोधेषु । ). व्रीडा-modesty. सुकविता-is used here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "in the sense of ‘good power of composition, poetic genius. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "लोभश्चेदगुणेन किं sl. 55, further on.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 22 दाक्षिण्यं—generosity, kindness. Cf. दक्षिणा परिजने S'ak.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and दाक्षिण्यरूढेन Rag. 1. 31. शाठ्य—शठस्य भावः । This is to pay",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tit for tat. नयः—politic behaviour; a conduct of policy. आर्जवम्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "rectitude, straightforwardness. धूर्तता—cautiousness, shrewdness.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "लोकस्थितिः—stability or preservation of social order.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 23. सिञ्चति वाचि सत्यम्—a curious phrase. It means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "‘causes men to be always truthful’. सत्यं-सति साधु. सत् + यत् ,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "दिशति brings about; lit. grants. प्रसादयति—purifies, enlightens.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कथय—cf the similar use of ‘say’ in English poetry. Cf दूरीकरोति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "कुमतिं विमलीकरोति चेतश्चिरंतनमघं चुलुकीकरोति । भूतेषु किं च करुणां बहु-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "लीकरोति संगः सतां किमु न मङ्गलमातनोति ॥ Bhám. Vil. I. 119; also",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "महाजनस्य संसर्गः कस्य नोन्नतिकारकः; सतां हि संगः सकलं प्रसूते &c.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Fig—In the last line there is अर्थान्तरन्यास अलंकार. There is also",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "दीपकालंकार ( कारकदीपक ) in the first three lines, सैव ( सकृद्वृत्तिः )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "क्रियासु बह्वीषु कारकस्येति दीपकम् When a case noun occurring once",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
